# Sensitive files
*-base64.txt
*api-key*.txt
*certificate*.txt

# Sprite retouching. Plates are regenerated from the footage by
# `technique-sprites.mjs --export-masks`, so they are never worth committing.
# Edited masks ARE worth keeping — they are the only record of a hand fix, and
# without them a rebuild silently reverts to the automatic result.
retouch/*.plate.png
retouch/*.psd

# The source footage lives here too, at three quarters of a gigabyte. It is the
# one irreplaceable input and it does not belong in git.
retouch/*.mp4

# `netlify dev` artifacts. The CLI adds .netlify itself; deno.lock comes from
# the Edge Functions runtime it boots and is equally local-only.
.netlify
deno.lock

# Logo build sources: keep the layered PSD local, as with retouch/*.psd.
# The lockup is generated from assets-src/*.png + the vendored font.
assets-src/*.psd
scripts/__pycache__/

# Store screenshots: regenerated by scripts/store-shots.mjs in one command,
# ~20MB a shoot. Upload artefacts, not source.
assets-src/store/

# Social cards: 70 PNGs regenerated by `npm run social:cards` in one command,
# from data already tracked in techniqueLibrary.ts. Same reasoning as the
# store shots — output, not source. captions.md is regenerated with them.
assets-src/social/

# Parked art: the shirt/QR merch that was never used, and the silhouette and
# sprite-edge captures from reviewing the v1.15.0 sprites. Unlike the two
# above these are not regenerable — they are kept on disk deliberately — but
# they are not app assets and were shipping from public/ until they were moved
# here. Ignored so they stop reading as untracked work.
assets-src/merch/
assets-src/audits/
